ect a Size\nL80: \nL81: Change View\nL82: \nL83: Size/SKU  | Availability  | Price\nL84: --- | --- | ---\nL85: \nL86: * * *\nL87: ### About This Item\nL88: \nL89: CAS Number:\nL90: \nL91: 【9†84082-64-4】\nL92: \nL93: UNSPSC Code:\nL94: \nL95: 12352202\nL96: \nL97: EC Number:\nL98: \nL99: 282-010-7\nL100: \nL101: NACRES:\nL102: \nL103: NA.61\nL104: \nL105: MDL number:\nL106: \nL107: 【10†MFCD00131629】\nL108: \nL109: Form:\nL110: \nL111: partially purified powder\nL112: \nL113: Biological source:\nL114: \nL115: Porcine stomach\nL116: \nL117: Pricing and availability is not currently available.\nL118: \nL119: Technical Service\nL120: \nL121: Need help? Our team of experienced scientists is here for you.\nL122: \nL123: 【11†Let Us Assist】\nL124: \nL125: * * *\nL126: \nL127: * * *\nL128: \nL129: Properties\nL130: \nL131: ### biological source\nL132: \nL133: Porcine stomach\nL134: \nL135: ### Quality Segment\nL136: \nL137: 【12†200】\nL138: \nL139: ### type\nL140: \nL141: Type III\nL142: ### form\nL143: \nL144: partially purified powder\nL145: \nL146: ### composition\nL147: \nL148: bound sialic acid, 0.5-1.5%\nL149: \nL150: ### technique(s)\nL151: \nL152: microbiological culture: suitable\nL153: \nL154: ### solubility\nL155: \nL156: NaOH: soluble 20 mg/mL\nL157: \nL158: ### storage temp.\nL159: \nL160: 2-8°C\nL161: \nL162: Description\nL163: \nL164: ### General description\nL165: \nL166: Mucins or mucus glycoproteins are the main macromolecular components of mammalian mucus. It was also used in a study to evaluate the sputum smears concentrated by cyto-centrifugation for detection of acid-fast bacilli.\nL167: ### Application\nL168: \nL169: Mucin from porcine stomach was used in studies on the binding site of the galactose-specific agglutinin PA-IL from Pseudomonas aeruginosa.\nL170: \nL171: ### Biochem/physiol Actions\nL172: \nL173: Mucus forms the protective cover for all epithelial surfaces. The major structural component of mucus is gel-forming mucins. The mucus layer covering the intestinal epithelium has the MUC2 mucin as its central molecule. MUC2 is produced by goblet cells.\nL174: ### Preparation Note\nL175: \nL176: Prepared according to the method of Glenister, et al., for use in complex growth media for dental plaque bacteria.\nL177: \nL178: * * *\nL179: \nL180: ## Compare Similar Items\nL181: \nL182: 【13†View Full Comparison】\nL183: \nL184: * * *\nL185: \nL186: Show Differences\nL187: \nL188: [Input]\nL189: \nL190: 1 of 1\nL191: ###### This Item\nL192:  | M2378  | A1830  | SRE0027\nL193: --- | --- | --- | ---\nL194: 【14†Sigma-Aldrich M1778 Mucin from porcine stomach】[Button: Quick View]  | 【15†Sigma-Aldrich M2378 Mucin from porcine stomach】[Button: Quick View]  | 【16†Sigma-Aldrich A1830 Albumin from porcine serum】[Button: Quick View]  | 【17†Sigma-Aldrich SRE0027 Heparin sodium porcine mucosa】[Button: Quick View]\nL195: description Type III, bound sialic acid 0.5-1.5 %, partially purified powder  | description Type II  | description lyophilized powder, ≥98% (agarose gel electrophoresis)  | description-\nL196: technique(s)microbiological culture: suitable  | technique(s)cell culture | mammalian: suitable  | technique(s)cell culture | mammalian: suitable  | technique(s)-\nL197: biological source Porcine stomach  | biological source Porcine stomach  | biological source Porcine  | biological source Porcine (mucosa)\nL198: form partially purified powder  | form powder  | form lyophilized powder  | form powder\nL199: solubility NaOH: soluble 20 mg/mL  | solubility 1 M NaOH: soluble 20 mg/mL  | solubility-  | solubility water: 50 mg/mL (colorless to faint yellow)\nL200: storage temp.2-8°C  | storage temp.2-8°C  | storage temp.2-8°C  | storage temp.-\nL201: Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 200  | Quality Level 300  | Quality Level 400\nL202: * * *\nL203: ### Still not finding the right product?\nL204: \nL205: Explore all of our products under 【18†Mucin from porcine stomach】\nL206: \nL207: 【18†View All Products】\nL208: \nL209: * * *\n