years ago\nL294: \nL295: Mucins are soluble in water, forming hazy viscous solutions.\nL296: \nL297: Helpful?\nL298: \nL299: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL300: \nL301: [Button: Report ]\nL302: \nL303:   2. Anonymous\nL304: \nL305: · 4 years ago\nL306: \nL307: What are the differences between Mucin from porcine stomach Products M2378 and M1778?\nL308: \nL309: 1 answer\nL310: \nL311:     1. Technical Support\nL312: \nL313: · 4 years ago\nL314: Product No. M2378 is a crude mucin preparation. Product No. M1778 is a partially purified powder prepared according to the method described in Glenister, D.A. and Salmon. K. Microbial Ecol. in Health & Disease 1, 31, (1988). The amount of bound sialic acids are also different. Please refer to the specification sheets on our website.\nL315: \nL316: Helpful?\nL317: \nL318: Yes · 1 No · 1\nL319: \nL320: [Button: Report ]\nL321: \nL322:   3. Anonymous\nL323: \nL324: · 4 years ago\nL325: \nL326: How can I solubilize Product M1778, Mucin from porcine stomach?\nL327: \nL328: 1 answer\nL329:     1. Technical Support\nL330: \nL331: · 4 years ago\nL332: \nL333: Mucin is not readily soluble in aqueous solutions. Turbid \"solutions\" will form at about 5 mg/mL in 0.1 M acetate buffer, pH 5.0. To try to increase the solubility, one might try further dilution and sonication, but we have not tried this in our labs.\nL334: \nL335: Helpful?\nL336: \nL337: Yes · 1 No · 0\nL338: \nL339: [Button: Report ]\nL340: \nL341:   4. Anonymous\nL342: \nL343: · 4 years ago\nL344: \nL345: What is the Department of Transportation shipping information for this product?\nL346: \nL347: 1 answer\nL348: \nL349:     1. Technical Support\nL350: \nL351: · 4 years ago\nL352: Transportation information can be found in Section 14 of the product's (M)SDS.To access the shipping information for this material, use the link on the product detail page for the product.\nL353: \nL354: Helpful?\nL355: \nL356: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL357: \nL358: [Button: Report ]\nL359: \nL360:   5. Anonymous\nL361: \nL362: · 4 years ago\nL363: \nL364: Is Product M1778, Mucin from porcine stomach, a purified preparation of mucin?\nL365: \nL366: 1 answer\nL367: \nL368:     1. Technical Support\nL369: \nL370: · 4 years ago\nL371: This product is a partially purified preparation of mucin based on the method of Glenister cited on the product's webpage.\nL372: \nL373: Helpful?\nL374: \nL375: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL376: \nL377: [Button: Report ]\nL378: \nL379:   6. Anonymous\nL380: \nL381: · 4 years ago\nL382: \nL383: What does the \"Type\" designation in Mucin from porcine stomach mean?\nL384: \nL385: 1 answer\nL386: \nL387:     1. Technical Support\nL388: \nL389: · 4 years ago\nL390: \nL391: The type designation does not have any particular biological significance.  It is used to emphasize differences in the listings of this product.\nL392: \nL393: Helpful?\nL394: \nL395: Yes · 3 No · 0\nL396: [Button: Report ]\nL397: \nL398:   7. Anonymous\nL399: \nL400: · 4 years ago\nL401: \nL402: What is the molecular weight of Product M1778, Mucin from porcine stomach?\nL403: \nL404: 1 answer\nL405: \nL406:     1. Technical Support\nL407: \nL408: · 4 years ago\nL409: \nL410: This product is partially purified from crude mucin, M2378.  Sigma has not determined the molecular weight of this product. Neither has the sugar and amino acid composition been determined.\nL411: \nL412: Helpful?\nL413: \nL414: Yes · 0 No · 0\nL415: \nL416: [Button: Report ]\nL417: \nL418: ★★★★★ ★★★★★ No rating value for Mucin from porcine stomach\nL419: Search topics and reviews ϙ [Input: Search topics and reviews] Search topics and reviews ✘ Clear Search field ϙ Search\nL420: \nL421:   * 【22†0 Reviews】\nL422:   * 【22†7 Questions】\nL423:   * 【22†7 Answers】\nL424: ## Reviews\nL425: \nL426: ★★★★★ No rating value Be the first to review this product . This action will open a modal dialog.\nL427: \nL428: ▼ Rating Filter by Rating\nL429: \nL430: Filter by Rating [Select]\nL431: \nL432: ▼ Locale Filter by Locale\nL433: \nL434: Filte